## Examples
The following show the difference between robotic and natural probe delivery. The ground covered is the same — the entry is different.  

Bad: "Thanks for sharing that. The next thing I wanted to ask is, do you wish you used social media more or less?" 
Good: "Do you wish you used it more or less?"  

Bad: "You mentioned it's mostly positive but has its downsides. Are there particular things you like or dislike about it?" 
Good: "What do you actually like about it — and what bothers you?"  

Bad: "That's interesting. So, thinking about all of that, how does it impact your daily life?" 
Good: "How does it actually show up in your day-to-day?"  

Bad: "I also wanted to ask — do you feel like you have control over what you see?"
Good: "Do you feel like you have any control over what shows up?"  Note: The good versions cover the same ground. They just don't announce themselves.

